course: dictionary
lesson: 10661
title: Unknown and the unknown
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unknown is a word with two jobs. As an adjective it describes a thing: «If a number you do not know calls or messages you, let a parent answer or ignore it.» An unknown number is one you do not know.
explain: As a noun, the unknown means everything we do not know yet. «Explorers travelled into the unknown and brought back descriptions, so mapmakers could fill in the gaps bit by bit.» Each description filled a gap, so the unknown got a little smaller.
explain: In maths, the unknown is the number you are trying to find. «The unknown number plus 5 is 12» tells you the missing number is 7, because you work back from what is given. Look at the words around unknown to see which job it is doing.
fact: Unknown (adjective) means not known, as in an unknown number, or not famous, as in an unknown singer.
fact: The unknown (noun) is everything we do not know yet, like a journey into the unknown.
fact: In maths, the unknown is the number to be found, often shown as a letter like x or as a box.
fact: «Unknowns» is the plural noun, meaning several things we do not know yet.
fact: «Duōshao» means how many or how much: «duōshao qián?» is how much money?
exercise: In «an unknown singer», what does unknown mean? | *Not famous | Very old | Lost in the crowd | Loud and famous
exercise: In maths, what is the unknown? | A number too big to count | The answer you already have | *A letter or box for the number you must find | A sign that means add
exercise: «Explorers travelled into the unknown.» What is the unknown here? | A small, quiet room | A type of food | The sea at night, which is always the same | *Places nobody has explored or mapped yet
test: «Unknown numbers are best answered by a parent, or not at all.» What should you do with an unknown number? | *Let a parent answer it, or ignore it | Answer it yourself and give your address | Call it back straight away | Write its digits on your hand
test: In «duōshao qián?», what does duōshao ask about? | What colour something is | Who did something | How far away something is | *How many or how much
exam: Which sentence uses unknown as a noun? | «An unknown bottle sat on the table.» | *«We sailed into the unknown.» | «An unknown visitor knocked on the door.»
